    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c06809d1-82f7-56ab-93c7-0c9d5efbc5a2",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the line integral of $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{- y - z}{x}$ along the curve\n\n$$\n\\mathbf r(t)=\\langle t,t^{2},\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\rangle,\\qquad 1\\le t\\le \\sqrt{3}.\n$$\n\nGive the exact value.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To calculate the line integral, we will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s &=\\int_a^b f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\mathbf{r}(t)=(t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k}$, then along the curve we have $x=t$, $y=t^{2}$, $z=\\frac{t^{2}}{2}$.\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf{r}'(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t^{2})\\,\\mathbf{j}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\  & =(1)\\,\\mathbf{i}+(2 t)\\,\\mathbf{j}+(t)\\,\\mathbf{k} \\\\ \\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\| & =\\sqrt{\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2+\\left(\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}t}\\right)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^2+(2 t)^2+(t)^2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5 t^{2} + 1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{- y - z}{x}$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{(-1)[(t^{2})+\\left(\\frac{t^{2}}{2}\\right)]}{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)t^2}{(1)t} \\\\  & =- \\frac{3 t}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int_C f\\,\\text{d}s \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\,\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\left(- \\frac{3 t}{2}\\right)(\\sqrt{5 t^{2} + 1})\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this using the substitution $u=5 t^{2} + 1$, $\\text{d}u=(10 t)\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & ={\\int }_{6}^{16}\\sqrt{u}\\cdot - \\frac{3}{20}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =- \\frac{3}{20}{\\int }_{6}^{16}u^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =- \\frac{3}{20}\\cdot\\frac{2}{3}u^{3/2}\\big|_{6}^{16} \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{10}[(16)^{3/2}-(6)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =- \\frac{1}{10}[(64)-(6 \\sqrt{6})] \\\\  & =\\left(- \\frac{32}{5}\\right)-\\left(- \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6}}{5}\\right) \\\\  & =- \\frac{32}{5} + \\frac{3 \\sqrt{6}}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "ff2a2f03-fc3e-5591-ab6c-1e7aae4349d6",
